{"term":"trail","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:81a2eb7f063beb8fb3","definition":"To follow behind (someone or something); to tail (someone or something).","example":"The hunters trailed their prey deep into the woods.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["mistrail","trail away","trail behind","trailer","trailing","trail net","trail off","untrailed"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trail#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7ba8acd2c34bf951a3","definition":"To drag (something) behind on the ground.","example":"You'll get your coat all muddy if you trail it around like that.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["mistrail","trail away","trail behind","trailer","trailing","trail net","trail off","untrailed"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trail#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5bc82b6b8f5f8815e1","definition":"To leave (a trail of).","example":"He walked into the house, soaking wet, and trailed water all over the place.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["mistrail","trail away","trail behind","trailer","trailing","trail net","trail off","untrailed"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trail#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e1567734785484dc7c","definition":"To show a trailer of (a film, TV show etc.); to release or publish a preview of (a report etc.) in advance of the full publication.","example":"His new film was trailed on TV last night.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["mistrail","trail away","trail behind","trailer","trailing","trail net","trail off","untrailed"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trail#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3dbb79df5b35d80929","definition":"To hang or drag loosely behind; to move with a slow sweeping motion.","example":"The bride's long dress trailed behind her as she walked down the aisle.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["mistrail","trail away","trail behind","trailer","trailing","trail net","trail off","untrailed"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trail#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b374dbcb707c262f25","definition":"To run or climb like certain plants.","example":"The flowers glowed red and golden: snapdragons and sunflowers, and nasturtians trailing all over the turf walls and peeping in at the round windows.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["mistrail","trail away","trail behind","trailer","trailing","trail net","trail off","untrailed"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trail#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:94b4698b4b5a522134","definition":"To drag oneself lazily or reluctantly along.","example":"Our parents marched to church and we trailed behind.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["mistrail","trail away","trail behind","trailer","trailing","trail net","trail off","untrailed"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trail#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a9717aa8f7385d63b7","definition":"To be losing, to be behind in a competition.","example":"Neil Lennon and his players have, in almost no time at all, roared back from trailing Rangers by 15 points in November to ending the year two points clear.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["mistrail","trail away","trail behind","trailer","trailing","trail net","trail off","untrailed"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trail#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f3cc9f78c758573197","definition":"To carry (a firearm) with the breech near the ground and the upper part inclined forward, the piece being held by the right hand near the middle.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["mistrail","trail away","trail behind","trailer","trailing","trail net","trail off","untrailed"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trail#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7b9c4cd5bf9cb06e81","definition":"To create a trail in.","example":"The sun shone on burnished bodies and arm-bands, and robes of beaver trailed the grass as majestic fellows trod back and forth in the passion of eloquence.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["mistrail","trail away","trail behind","trailer","trailing","trail net","trail off","untrailed"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trail#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8544123322e1a4323c","definition":"To travel by following or creating trails.","example":"Trailed three miles down the North side and encamped early, making thirteen miles trailed to-day.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["mistrail","trail away","trail behind","trailer","trailing","trail net","trail off","untrailed"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trail#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:4d672efb528a2109ef","definition":"To transport (livestock) by herding it along a trail.","example":"One operator on the Boise Forest in Idaho reports that where he formerly marketed 80-pound lambs after trailing them 10 days from the allotment, his lambs now often tip the scales at 100 pounds or better, mainly because only one day is required to transport an entire shipment to the railroad through the use of truck pullmans.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["mistrail","trail away","trail behind","trailer","trailing","trail net","trail off","untrailed"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trail#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:24c7741ece8aeae5f6","definition":"To take advantage of the ignorance of; to impose upon.","example":"I presently perceived she was (what is vernacularly termed) trailing Mrs. Dent; that is, playing on her ignorance.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"dated","register":"dated","wordFamily":["mistrail","trail away","trail behind","trailer","trailing","trail net","trail off","untrailed"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trail#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:15e9d240faa9b6195b","definition":"The track or indication marking the route followed by something that has passed, such as the footprints of animal on land or the contrail of an airplane in the sky.","example":"The trail has gone cold.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["spoor","sign"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["mistrail","trail away","trail behind","trailer","trailing","trail net","trail off","untrailed","path","track"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trail#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:49f051d40a34b518c9","definition":"A route for travel over land, especially a narrow, unpaved pathway for use by hikers, horseback riders, etc.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":["dirt track","footpath","path","track"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["mistrail","trail away","trail behind","trailer","trailing","trail net","trail off","untrailed","path","track"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trail#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:984f5c66620c54d503","definition":"A route or circuit generally.","example":"Politicians are on the campaign trail in preparation for this year's election.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["mistrail","trail away","trail behind","trailer","trailing","trail net","trail off","untrailed","path","track"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trail#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7fdea4cbb9f1bcbe18","definition":"A trailer broadcast on television for a forthcoming film or programme.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["mistrail","trail away","trail behind","trailer","traili